%description:

Tcp.receiveBufferSize:limiting -- host2 takes 5 segments, 7240 bytes of the data beyond its offer.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "the receive buffer, apart from the advertised window (Linux sk_rcvbuf):
the unread data and the out-of-order data use it, and the offered window is the smaller of its
free space and the advertised window less the unread data; -1B: the buffer is the advertised
window".

The classes: none (-1B, the default: the buffer is the advertised window), limiting (a value
below advertisedWindow: the offer is at most the free buffer), ample (a value above
advertisedWindow, 131072B of LinuxTcp: the advertised window limits the offer, and the buffer
limits the data). The code: TcpConnection::hasEnoughSpaceForSegmentInReceiveQueue() accepts a
segment when it ends within the first unread byte plus the buffer;
TcpConnection::selectRcvWnd() offers the smaller of the free buffer and the advertised window
less the unread data. This test separates "limiting" from the other values.

Host under test: host2; host2 offers a window of 16384 bytes (advertisedWindow, a precondition), and its application
does not read. The tap writes 65535 into the window field of each segment of host2, so that
host1, which sends 50000 bytes, sends beyond the offer of host2. The 12th segment starts at
15928, within the window, and ends at 17376, beyond it. Observation: level 1, the highest ACK of host2 at 2 s acknowledges
5 segments, 7240 bytes: the buffer of 8192 bytes takes 5 segments; the 6th ends beyond it.

%# parameter: Tcp.receiveBufferSize
%# class: limiting
%# value: 8192B
%# key: *.host2.tcp.receiveBufferSize
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"
#include "TcpTestApp.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpReceiveBufferSizeLimiting")
        .intercept(tap("tap").from("host2").filterPacket("tcp.ackBit == true").set("tcp.window", "65535")
                     .describe("each segment of host2: the window field 65535, so that host1 sends beyond the offer of host2"))
        .act(action().at(0.0).run<TcpTestApp>("host2.app[0]", [](TcpTestApp& app) {
            app.socket().setAutoRead(false);
            app.socket().bind(1000);
            app.socket().listen();
        }))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
             .capture("isn", "tcp.sequenceNo")
             .describe("the SYN of host1")
             .within(0.5))
        .meanwhile(anyNumberOfTimes(on("host2.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
                                        .filterPacket("tcp.ackBit == true")
                                        .captureMax("highestAck", "tcp.ackNo")
                                        .within(3.0)))
        .act(action().at(2.0)
                 .describe("the highest ACK of host2")
                 .assertModule("host2.tcp.conn-*", "{highestAck} == {isn} + 1 + 7240"));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpReceiveBufferSizeLimiting compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host2.tcp.receiveBufferSize = 8192B    # the parameter under test
*.host2.app[0].typename = "TcpTestApp"
*.host2.tcp.advertisedWindow = 16384
*.host1.app[0].sendBytes = 50000B
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpReceiveBufferSizeLimiting: PASS
